cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or cite the preprint, please cite it as below."
title: "Subspace Anti-Phase Attention: Mitigating Strictly Positive Softmax Leakage via Orthogonal Subspace Phase Inversion"
authors:
  - name: "Huaiji Team"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-2312-6913"
    email: "contact@huaiji.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/3y3y3y-huaiji/mobius-attention"
url: "https://github.com/3y3y3y-huaiji/mobius-attention"
abstract: >-
  Standard Transformer self-attention normalizes dot products via strictly positive
  Softmax operators on the open probability simplex, causing premise distraction and
  attention leakage. We introduce Subspace Anti-Phase Attention (SG-Möbius-RoPE),
  an orthogonal subspace phase modulation framework extending RoPE with active noise
  cancellation principles to achieve exact destructive attention suppression and
  reversion without modifying historical key-value caches.
keywords:
  - "Transformer"
  - "Attention Mechanism"
  - "RoPE"
  - "Subspace Modulation"
  - "Active Noise Cancellation"
  - "Formal Verification"
  - "Lean 4"
  - "Long-Context LLMs"
license: "Apache-2.0"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
